# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the Clang + LLVM libomp + Archer build
# (tools/linux-macos/test.sh, #420). Archer (libarcher, loaded through
# OMP_TOOL_LIBRARIES) reports the OpenMP synchronization to TSan, so races in
# code run inside an OpenMP region are checked; only the uninstrumented
# runtimes are silenced.
#
# libomp's own mutexes (pthread_mutex_init in a worker vs pthread_mutex_lock on
# the main thread): libomp is not built with TSan. called_from_lib ignores the
# interceptors called from libomp itself only, not the outlined loop bodies it
# runs (verified: a race planted in an `omp parallel for` is still reported).
called_from_lib:libomp.so
#
# OpenBLAS pthreads workers (uninstrumented): reports whose stack passes
# through OpenBLAS, e.g. its threads' memset in dscal_k vs Armadillo reading the
# result on the calling thread after the BLAS call returned.
race:libopenblas
